                    insight_strong:         `Board convinced: you closed the EUR 45M gap, kept the cell-balancing IP in-house and off flagged borders, dual-sourced the main lane, and chose an entry mode that serves the live USD 90M pipeline and qualifies for incentives. The plan is different from 2019 on every axis that failed — and it degraded gracefully when the shock hit.`,
                    insight_ipleak:         `2019, again: you offshored the core cell-balancing IP to chase the saving. The board lived through exactly this — defects, a design leak, and a 6–8 point margin hit as the design is copied. Whatever cost you recovered is borrowed against the pricing power that recovers it.`,
                    insight_concentrated:   `Savings found, resilience zero: you hit the number through one concentrated lane in a flagged jurisdiction. One export-control listing and the whole footprint stalls. The cheapest plan was the most fragile one — a second source was the missing line.`,
                    insight_short:          `The plan did not fully reconcile. Savings, control, market fit and resilience still pull in different directions — enough that the live shock and the board's 2019 memory found the seam.`,
                    insight_savings_short:  `You fell short of the EUR 45M target. At a 9% operating margin the price cut erases EUR 38–57M of contribution; under-recovering here means the margin does not come back and the customers dual-source anyway.`,
                    insight_savings_hit:    `You cleared the EUR 45M cost-recovery target — the margin the price cut threatened is restored, provided the saving was realised and not just claimed on a slipping quality-ramp.`,
                    insight_market_weak:    `The US entry under-served the live pipeline: too slow, too policy-exposed, or under-committed. A USD 90M order book that a rival exports into first is a one-time loss, not a delay.`,
                    insight_trusted:        `Control is high and the footprint is resilient — the cost was recovered without mortgaging the IP. That is the difference between closing a gap and repeating 2019, and it is exactly the answer the board wanted to hear.`,

                    hint_ipleak:            `The cell-balancing IP is offshore or in third-party hands — the 2019 configuration. Pull it back in-house and onshore: the margin advantage that funds everything else is that IP.`,
